The attached image illustrates flow cytometry results demonstrating that Nano-11 enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel A, showing dot plots of OVA versus Nano-11 fluorescence, indicates minimal uptake of soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone, but a substantial increase in both when BMDCs are incubated with Nano-11+OVA complexes. Panel B, a histogram of FITC-OVA fluorescence, further quantifies this, illustrating a significant rightward shift (increased fluorescence) for BMDCs treated with Nano-11+OVA compared to OVA or Nano-11 alone, confirming enhanced intracellular antigen delivery.